  "inventory_findings": [
    "Global cast-versus-mask probes included all four defining expressions, but used the old shared int local declaration. Explicit SUB masks alone retained the 222-instruction / XOR3 / MOVZX6 stage.",
    "The old short-local mask controls started from ADD-mask / SUB-cast source. They did not test the three explicit subtraction masks in the all-short AMP scope. Their 219-instruction / XOR6 / MOVZX1 result is already known.",
    "No archived full-source probe changed the four first-stage sum scalings from multiplication by 2/4 to shifts by 1/2. The older add64shift candidate changed the separate Mp3Add helper accumulator and is unrelated to these scalar expressions.",
    "None of the four audited zero-producing expressions itself multiplies by a power of two: they are three wrapped differences and one wrapped sum. The neighboring scalings share c10/c11 or c14/c15 inputs, allowing a concrete optimizer-context comparison.",
    "The prior split-helper parameter probe covered short, int and unsigned int, with a short-local control for each. Unsigned-short parameter was absent. Earlier unsigned-short helper probes changed return types, not this parameter.",
    "No coefficient high-word packing multiplication control was found. The three factors are formed before the inner transform loop at A04D/A066/A077 and retained in separate stack slots. This inventory records the gap without treating it as an explanation for the four later zeroes."
  ],
